docs/decisions.md:1196:| OD81 | <a id="od81"></a>`ghost let` in the grammar (added 2026-10-30, item C4 of the owner picks of that day). Question: Whether the grammar gains the proof-only binding `ghost let` (with `ghost` a contextual keyword). Options: (a) add it to the grammar; (b) remove it from the parser, so the language loses the form; (c) keep the recorded divergence for now. Pick (the coordinator's pick after the Kimi, Codex and Grok review of 2026-10-30, a recommendation and not a decision): individual review required; no pick recorded. Austral: not applicable | the parser accepts it | CON-4, SYN-1 | decided 2026-11-01 by the owner (final set): Add, with `ghost` reserved |
