codex
The reconstruction proof exposed a defect in `WellFormed`: it checked blocks through lookup, but `fromExposed` scans every list entry. Contradictory entries under one identity could therefore evade its checks. I added an invariant requiring every stored entry to agree with lookup, and proved allocation preserves it. Under that invariant, reconstruction’s in-bounds-first, then one-past rule is now proved.
